        <p>(10UNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.—The k) SANITARY WORKS 001IMITTBII of the County Borough of Warrington Allll PRIIPAIIIID TO 11BORIVII TIINDBRS for the supply of rhe following materials for a period of 12 months, or as the Committee may determine, from the first day of April next. CLHANSING DRPARTMENT. Bolts, Nuts and Washers, Brushes. Disinfectants. Hoop Iron, Wrought Iron, Cobra Oil, Wheelwright's Timber, Horse Hire, Workmen's Slops, Provender, and Steel Ashbins and Pails. Samples of goods required may be seen. and specification and form of Tender obtained from th 9 office of the Cleansing Superintendent, Central Sanitary Depet, Warrington, on payment of les. per section (itch payment.to be made at the Borough Treasurer's Office. Sankey-street) which will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Contractors whose tenders are accepted shall pay all persons engaged by them on the works the rate of wages recognised in the district, and shall observe such hours of labour as are generally accepted as fair in each trade. Tenders, addressed to " The Chairman of the Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington." endorsed " Nightsoil Department—Materials " and securely fastened, must be delivered not later than Monday, March lit, 1909. Samples to be sent with tender. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. JAMBS J. A. PARFITT. M. Inst. C.S. Cleansing Superintendent. Cleansing Department, Warrington. February 10th, 1909.</p>
