      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-02-13_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>PENKETH.</head>
        <p>PENKETH.</p>
        <p>iturP24it Llllll.lll INSTITUTE.—The members of the above i'.“l held their first annual whist drive and dance corn rLd43' in the new Council schools, Stock's-lane, And 11:',„"cing at eight o'clock. A good number attended tenti:"°st:Pleasant evening was spent. The winning tiro p Wore—Messrs. F. Dendy, W. Barker and W. ebeceteutirst ; winning ladies—Miss Cooper, Mists bient,7Bwere 433, Mrs. Newbold and Mrs. Dendy. The refresh- ;d supplied by Mrs. Routledge. Dr. - Murray, MM M.C. for dancing, the music being pro- kepto;Y 14. r. Ta7lor'5 string band. The dancing Was unil t 1 o clock when all made their way home Pleamed with the evening's enjoyment.</p>
