        <head>MARRIED WOMEN TEACHERS</head>
        <p>MARRIED WOMEN TEACHERS</p>
        <p>A Drastic Proposal.</p>
        <p>At Monclare meeting of the Education CODIIIIitiga Mr. T. P. BradAaw will move :—" That the lianagers of public elementary schools-and the School Manage- ment Committee be instructed to give three months' notice in writing to terminate, on the last day of June, J 999. the engagements of all nurried female teachers *resent on their staffs, and that, after that date, this Aufhbrity will not recognise nor pay the salary of ftew liried female teacher.'</p>
        <p>Alderman Ellison's Golden Wedding. Alderman and Abs. Ellison celebrated their goldett wedd'fng on Sunday,. and were the recipients of nnmerous.telegrams and letters of cono.ratulation on the happy anniversary. ?ambers of the family joined in a quiet but very pleasant celebration and the good wishes extended to Alderman and Mrs. Ellison will be hearilyre,echoed by a very wide circle of towns- people.</p>
