        <p>An irate female seeks admittance to the editor's sanctum. "But I tell you, madam," protests the clerk, "that the editor is too busy to talk to anyone to-day." She eyed him up and down for s few minutes, then exclaimed: "Never mind; you let me in. I shan't trouble him much in that respect, for I'll do the talking." •</p>
