      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-02-13_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <head>LANCASHIRE CONGREGATIONAL UNION.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE CONGREGATIONAL UNION.</p>
        <p>Liverpool District.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting was held in Great George-street' Chapel, last week. After devotional exercises the district treasurer (Mr. E. Sherrock Eccles) took the chair. He referred in touching terms to the death of the late general treasurer (Mr. H. Higson), and expressed; the pleasure with which they all welcomed Mr. W. J. Boothroyd to that post. Ile asked for larger contri- butions from the churches to sustain the important work ,9arried on by the union. The following officers for the year were elected :—Chairman, the Rev. G. E. Cheeseman, who is also this year chairman of the County Union; trensurer, Mr. E. Shorrock Eccles; secretary, the Rev. J. Youge ; executive, the Revs. G. A. Brock, W. M. Rawlinson, C. F. Richardson, and 0. L. Roberts, and Messrs. G. 0. Jones, J. B. Leach and J. Jackson • representatives on the Council of the Congregational' Union of England ' and Wales, the Revs. G. E. Cheesemau, R. H. Sewell and John Yonge. and Messrs. B. Aspinall G. Oliver Jones, J. B. Leach, Colonel W. W. Pilkington, and W. J. Boothroyd. The following new ministers were received :—The Revs. A. H. Fowler, J. Gardiner, J. W. Johnston, A. J. Lee, .Pandy Thotas, and A. H. VChiteley Transfers were granted to the Revs. Dr. Owen Evans, T. Maine and V. M. Arthur. The followina grants were made to aided churches : —Howe Bridge, £5O; Berkley-street, £5O; Rice-lane, £35; Woolton, £35 ; Orrell, £5O; Skelmersdale, £6O ; Ainsdale, £5O; Canning-road Southport,.£3o; Hauipton- road, Southport, £6O; Cockhedge, IVarrington, £5O ; IVinnes, £4O ; Abram, £25; Pemberton, £4O. The new general secretary (the Rev. A. J. Viner) received a hearty welcome, and addressed the meeting. Tea was served in the schoolroom to the delegates, and the vote of thanks was responded to by the Rev. R. H. Sewell. On the invitation of the Rev. G. E. Chess- man, it was decided to hold the next annual meeting at Huy ton. .</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-02-13_WidnesExaminer_art0125" n="art0125">
        <head>BE YOUR OWN bOCTOR.</head>
        <p>BE YOUR OWN bOCTOR.</p>
        <p>If you are ailing you can save doctor's fees and cure yourself at a moderate cost. Afunyon's Home Doctor Book, tells how to treat yourself at home with shilling remedies obtained from any chemist. A copy of this book will be sent free (if The " Warrington Examiner" is mentioned) to anyone writing the Munyon Company, 61 New Oxford-street, London,W.C.</p>
      </div>
