        <p>MR. LOOIS HENSHALL. • Application for Ball Refused In London. We understand that Mr. Justice Bucknill, sitting in Chambers, has refused an application for bail to be granted to Mr. Louis Ileushall pending his trial at the Liverpool Assizes in March.</p>
        <p>SHOOTING IN SELF-DEFENCE. ITS Warrington Showmen Acquitted. At the Denbighshire Assizes on Thursday John Cook and his scns, James Cook and John Cook, showmen, of Longford-street, Warrington. were found not guilty and discharged on a charge of wounding several miners of Coedpoeth, near Wrexham. A riot occurred after a fair on November 7th, and showmen, who imagined they were in danger, fired with guns from shooting galleries upon a menacing crowd, wounding several. The show property was afterwards set on fire and £lOO worth of damage done. The jury found that the show- men acted in self-defence. Mr. Ellis Jones Griffiths, M.P., conducted the prosecution and Mt. Harrison (instructed by Mr. T. S. Steele, Warrington) defended.</p>
